    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Plage de la Salis is a long fine-sand beach at the foot of the Cap d'Antibes, famous for its backdrop view of the snow-capped Alps — one of the finest panoramas on the French Riviera.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>A municipal order bans dogs from the beach during the beach season, from mid-June to mid-September. Outside this period, dogs on a leash are welcome, and many locals walk their companions here. Remember to pick up after your dog and to keep an eye on their behaviour.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: come in May–June or September–October — the water is still great for swimming and the beach is far quieter than in high summer.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The old town of Antibes and its Provençal market are a few minutes away, as is the coastal path that runs along the Cap d'Antibes.</p>
